# VRAM Recovery & CPU-Offload Stability Plan

We have confirmed the "Stuck UI" was caused by a backend crash that left the GPU memory locked (Zombie VRAM). This plan implements a "Clean Start" protocol and offloads the landmark detection to the CPU to ensure the 1.5-hour film render stays stable.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Performance Trade-off**: Moving "Landmarks" to the CPU will make the initial 10-20 seconds of each chunk slightly slower, but it saves ~800MB of VRAM which is required for the actual Lip-Sync drawing (UNet). This prevents the current "OOM" (Out of Memory) crashes.

## Proposed Changes

### [Engine Core]

#### [NEW] [kill_orphans.ps1](file:///C:/just-dub-it2/scripts/kill_orphans.ps1)
- Create a PowerShell script to force-terminate all orphaned `python.exe` and `ffmpeg.exe` instances except for the main dashboard. This releases "stuck" VRAM handles.

### [MuseTalk Submodule]

#### [MODIFY] [preprocessing.py](file:///C:/just-dub-it2/tools/MuseTalk/musetalk/utils/preprocessing.py)
- Change `Wholebody` and `FaceAlignment` backends from `cuda` to `cpu`. 
- This takes advantage of your **AVX2 extensions** on the CPU to handle the math while the GPU stays fresh for the rendering stage.

### [Lipsync Module]

#### [MODIFY] [lipsync_musetalk.py](file:///C:/just-dub-it2/app/stages/lipsync_musetalk.py)
- **Automatic Cleanup**: Integrated a call to the "Zombie Killer" before every chunk.
- **Pre-flight verification**: Ensure at least 1.0GB of VRAM is free before starting `inference.py`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. **Purge Test**: Run the orphan-kill script and verify Task Manager shows GPU usage dropping back to ~0-200MB.
2. **Mini-Pipeline Test**: Run the 45s test from the UI.
    - Check for "[MuseTalk] landmarks on cpu" in logs.
    - Verify GPU memory usage stays below 3.5GB during rendering.

### Manual Verification
- Re-run the Dashboard and resume the 86-minute project.
- Verify that Chunk 12 passes the "Extracting Landmarks" phase successfully.
